+## Hardware And Model Facts (Roofline)
+
+Hardware — 4× Intel Arc Pro B70 (from Intel ARK / B-series overview):
+- 608 GB/s memory bandwidth per card; 32 GB; 367 INT8 pTOPS (XMX); Gen5 PCIe x16; **no XeLink** → TP collectives cross PCIe.
+- Aggregate TP4 bandwidth ≈ 2432 GB/s if perfectly utilized.
+
+Model — `nameistoken/Qwen3.6-35B-A3B-Quark-W8A8-INT8` (source: snapshot `config.json`):
+- `Qwen3_5Moe`, **256 experts / top-8**, 40 layers, hybrid **30 GDN (linear-attention) + 10 full-attention** (full every 4th), hidden 2048.
+- **`mtp_num_hidden_layers: 1` — the model ships with a native Multi-Token-Prediction head.** This is the natural high-acceptance draft source for verified speculation.
+- Quark W8A8: per-channel symmetric INT8 weights, per-channel **dynamic** INT8 activations.
+
+Roofline math:
+- Active ≈ 3 B params INT8 ≈ 3 GB/token; TP4-sharded ≈ 750 MB/rank; at 608 GB/s → **~1.23 ms weight-read floor per token**.
+- 200 tok/s = 5.000 ms/token budget → weights are only ~25% of budget. **200 tok/s is physically reachable.**
+- But measured `model_forward` ≈ 5.46 ms (4.4× the floor) and outside-forward ≈ 4.59 ms. The gap is **overhead** (MoE dispatch, GDN recurrent updates, collectives, sampler, host orchestration), not compute.
+
+Implication: the win is overhead removal + speculation that amortizes the weight-read floor across multiple emitted tokens.
