+## Why 200 tok/s Requires Speculation
+
+From `data/qwen36-c1-gap-budget-fullcandidate-20260613h.{json,md}`:
+
+- Current decode ≈ 10 ms/token; target 200 = 5.000 ms/token; required saving **5.056 ms/token (50.3%)**; required speedup **2.011×**.
+- `model_forward` ≈ 5.46 ms; outside-forward ≈ 4.59 ms. **Even driving `model_forward` to ~0 ms would not reach 200** unless outside-forward is also cut.
+- The W8A8 MoE layerlet, projected perfectly across all 40 layers, caps at **~172 tok/s** — still short of 200; measured endpoint A/B gain was only **+1.42%**.
+
+The only math that reaches 200 with zero quality drift:
+
+```
+effective_tok/s = base_tok/s × mean_draft_acceptance
+~100 tok/s base × ~2.0 mean acceptance ≈ 200 tok/s
+~140 tok/s base × ~1.5 mean acceptance ≈ 210 tok/s
+```
+
+Both multipliers require the two P0 correctness fixes below. Speculation amortizes the ~1.2 ms weight-read floor across multiple emitted tokens — that is *why* 200 is reachable, not just base-rate tuning.
