+## Phase 1 — Raise the single-token kernel floor (~100 → ~140–160 tok/s)
+
+Start only after P0a lands a safe base. With 256 experts/top-8 at batch=1, MoE is **dispatch-bound** (8 tiny GEMMs + permute/unpermute), not compute-bound.
+
+1. **Fix the layerlet color-canary offset/scale bug**, then **persistent resident W8A8 MoE layerlet**: descriptors, expert pointers, scales, scratch, route buffers resident per layer/rank; enqueue only the route command. One boundary route→quant→GEMM1→SiLU→quant2→GEMM2→gather→combine. Target the documented **189 µs/layer** (current ~315 µs). Synthetic harness already passes graph-replay parity (0.0 diff).
+2. **Real XPU graph-collective capture** to remove `VLLM_XPU_GRAPH_NOOP_COMM_CAPTURE=1`. Collective bytes are cheap (0.05–0.08 ms) but the **host-dispatch gap around the no-op comm** is not — and no-op comm capture is part of what makes forced-comm fragile (de-risks P0a). Requires a true XPU communicator graph-capture context.
+3. **Recover the sampler ~4 tok/s** with a genuinely-different XPU greedy reduction (custom op; all argmax/max/topk-family variants corrupt or cost ~4 tok/s).
+4. **GDN recurrent-decode kernel tuning** (causal conv-1d + SSM) only after P0a makes native GDN safe under load.
+
+Gate: each item passes the P0a deep gate independently; A/B vs adjacent control with ≥4 repeats.
+
+## Phase 2 — Verified speculation (the ≥200 multiplier)
+
+Stack on the Phase-1 base. Speculation amortizes the ~1.2 ms weight-read floor across multiple emitted tokens.
+
+1. **n-gram proposer first** (no draft model) — establish the verified-acceptance harness; measure real acceptance on representative prompts.
+2. **Native MTP head** (`mtp_num_hidden_layers: 1`) — the trained MTP head is the high-acceptance draft source and the right long-term proposer. Note: MTP-on-XPU is **not** in vLLM's validated XPU list, so expect compile/capture work; keep n-gram as fallback.
+3. **Tune k** (start 2, push toward 4) against measured mean acceptance; report per-position acceptance, verifier cost, rollback cost, output parity.
+
+Gate: token-ID parity vs no-spec oracle on the full quality suite + 512-repeat canaries, across a 4K/16K/32K context sweep.
