+## R5. Errors & pitfalls identified in past work (do not repeat)
+
+- **P0b misdiagnosis.** The COW root-cause note treated diagnostic-flag-induced predecessor-reemission as a deep commit bug and spun up an "escrow / transactional harness" plan. Verify the unsuppressed path first (R1). Per AGENTS.md benchmark-identity rule: diff launcher env for spec flags before concluding a spec bug.
+- **Shallow-gate confusion.** The 77–86 tok/s "quality_suite=passed" ablations were shallow (1–2 repeats); they fail the 4-repeat promotion gate at the same repeat windows as the unsafe lane. Treat any result without "4 warm p512/o512 repeats + 128+ JSON + 256+ color" as smoke, not validated.
+- **Layerlet synthetic-oracle blindness.** Diffing the layerlet against the offsets-reference will always read ~0.0 because they share ops. Use `ref_fused_moe` or `rows_per_expert` as the oracle (R3).
+- **Wrong-tree flag assumption.** `VLLM_XPU_INT8_MOE_MIXED_WORKSPACE` is read in vLLM (`xpu_moe.py:34`), not in `vllm-xpu-kernels`. A kernels rebuild alone cannot change its behavior.
+- **Harness drift (2026-06-14h).** Omitting `COMPILATION_CONFIG='{"cudagraph_mode":"PIECEWISE"}'` silently measured the graph-none class (~15 tok/s) and was misread as a regression. The `run-qwen36-ablation-candidate.sh` autoconfig fix exists; keep using it and record `COMPILATION_CONFIG` in every summary.
+- **`VLLM_XPU_GRAPH_NOOP_COMM_CAPTURE=0` startup failure.** `parallel_state.graph_capture` asserts `CudaCommunicator` (`parallel_state.py:565`); a true XPU communicator graph-capture context is a prerequisite for removing the no-op-comm workaround (ties to Phase 1 item 2).
